(BIOL 110 - Lecture 12: Photosynthesis) Tj
T* (Learning objectives) Tj
T* (- Describe the light-dependent reactions and the Calvin cycle.) Tj
T* (- Explain how C4 and CAM plants reduce photorespiration.) Tj
T* (Overview) Tj
T* (6 CO2 + 6 H2O + light energy -> C6H12O6 + 6 O2) Tj
T* (Photosynthesis happens in chloroplasts. The thylakoid membranes hold the pigments;) Tj
T* (the fluid around them is the stroma.) Tj
T* (Light-dependent reactions \(thylakoid membrane\)) Tj
T* (- Photosystem II absorbs light and splits water, releasing oxygen as a by-product.) Tj
T* (- Electrons flow through the electron transport chain to Photosystem I.) Tj
T* (- The proton gradient drives ATP synthase to make ATP.) Tj
T* (- Photosystem I passes electrons to NADP+, forming NADPH.) Tj
T* (Calvin cycle \(stroma\)) Tj
T* (- The enzyme RuBisCO fixes CO2 onto ribulose bisphosphate \(RuBP\).) Tj
T* (- ATP and NADPH from the light reactions reduce the products to G3P sugar.) Tj
T* (- Most G3P regenerates RuBP; one in six molecules leaves to build glucose.) Tj
T* (Photorespiration) Tj
T* (RuBisCO sometimes grabs O2 instead of CO2, wasting energy, especially when hot and dry.) Tj
T* (C4 plants \(corn, sugarcane\) concentrate CO2 in bundle sheath cells.) Tj
T* (CAM plants \(cacti, pineapple\) open stomata only at night to save water.) Tj
T* (Exam reminder: know the inputs and outputs of each stage.) Tj
